<h1 class="visually-hidden">About</h1>

<div class="prose">
  <div class="rail-label">What it is</div>
  <div class="prose-body">
    <p class="lede">
      AtlasLatino is a grassroots effort to give visibility to the work of
      Latin American researchers and practitioners, across security,
      machine learning, data science, and more.
    </p>
    <p>
      Entries are added and verified by hand. Contributions come in through
      open pull requests and issues on GitHub, and each one is checked
      before it goes live. AtlasLatino is not a ranking. Every entry is
      worth the same, and the list will always be incomplete.
    </p>

    <p class="prose-credit">Originally created by Verónica Valeros, August 2026.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="prose">
  <div class="rail-label">Support</div>
  <div class="prose-body">
    <p>
      AtlasLatino is a free, volunteer-run project. If you'd like to help
      keep it going, you can sponsor it on
      <a href="https://github.com/sponsors/verovaleros">GitHub Sponsors</a>
      or buy me a coffee on
      <a href="https://ko-fi.com/verovaleros">Ko-fi</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
